<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Moroccan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Moroccan War was fought in 1844 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, which had given refuge and support to the Algerian resistance leader Abd al-Qadir. A French fleet bombarded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essaouira">Mogador</a>, and Marshal Bugeaud defeated the Moroccan army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-isly">Battle of Isly</a> in August. The Treaty of Tangier obliged Morocco to stop supporting Abd al-Qadir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-moroccan-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Moroccan War" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ch. Hugo, Amédée R. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bombardement_de_Tanger_en_aout_1844.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
